4. Interface presets and the C2M template
-----------------------------------------

The 802.3dj C2M preset starts from an 802-COM config template, shipped
unchanged, byte for byte, with its own License Notice sheet:

  sicopr_assist/data/templates/config_com-4p13p0_802p3dj_d2p3_200G_C2M_TP0_TP2_Egress_26_01_27.xlsx
  from opensource.ieee.org/802-com/com_code, tag 4.17.0
  (SHA-256 57e9da3f17dee495f386622f2bab30895a55b2ed40f2df997636d1a73af62e6e)

The preset values in sicopr_assist/data/presets.csv that come from the
802-COM C2C, CR and C2M templates and from the starting workbooks name that
source in their own row. Those workbooks are:

  Copyright 2025 802-COM Authors
  SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause

Values whose only source is a document that may not be redistributed (IEEE
Std 802.3ck-2022, IEEE P802.3dj drafts, the IEEE COM 3.70 workbooks, OIF
Implementation Agreements) are not in this repository. SiCoPR-Assist reads
them from a local overlay file the user names in the settings
(preset_overlay); without it, the presets that need them stop and say so.
